# Exp 8 — induct-quest-no-human: the run with no human in it

## TL;DR

Owner-ruled follow-up (2026-11-15, after a red-chair
pass). Owner-renamed 2026-11-15: was induct-solo; solo named no dimension. `/induct-quest-no-human <quest>...` runs the conductor with
no human present — overnight, for quests that are
already fleshed out and mechanical. It queues several
quests, rides cycles per Exp 6, and never pages, never
attests, never promotes. Blocked work parks in the
inbox for the morning. Its only output is the dawn
report.

## Diagram

```text
/induct-quest-no-human Q1 Q2 Q3
  preflight each quest --fail--> reported, not queued
  queue -> conductor per quest (desks only)
    needs_fix -> next cycle        (Exp 6 rule)
    blocked   -> PARK in inbox, quest stops, queue moves on
    cap hit   -> PARK, queue moves on
    landed    -> exp_fin, next exp
  budget hit -> queue stops, report says so
  dawn report: exp_fin list, parked inbox, tokens, sweep
```

## Pseudocode

```python
def no_human(quests, budget):
    for q in quests:
        if not preflight(q): report(q, "not queued"); continue
        while budget.left and (exp := next_exp(q)):
            step = dispatch_by_state(exp)      # never attest/page
            if exp.state == "blocked": park(q, exp); break
    return dawn_report()   # exp_fin, parked, usage sums, worktree sweep
```

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Intent | mechanical quests finish overnight; judgment waits for morning |
| Lane | standard (skill change; own exp per rule 6.6) |
| Output | new alias skill `skills/induct-quest-no-human/SKILL.md` (pointer to induct + no-human rails); no-human rules in `skills/induct/SKILL.md` where they generalize; installed copies |
| Depends on | Exp 6 (cycle autonomy), Exp 7 (report words) |

## Acceptance (fails today: no induct-quest-no-human exists)

| Case | Expected |
|---|---|
| human edges | solo never attests (`BP3_DECIDER` unset by it), never takes `resume`/`delete`, never pages a question |
| blocked exp mid-queue | exp parks with its inbox reason; its quest stops; the next queued quest still runs |
| preflight | a quest with an exp missing Acceptance rows, an open design question in any EXPERIMENT.md, or a red `make check` is not queued and is reported with the failed check named |
| budget | queue stops at the stated Run budget; the dawn report says the budget stopped it |
| quest_fin | solo never promotes or pushes; promotion stays the owner gate from Exp 7 |
| dawn report | per quest: exps at `exp_fin`, parked inbox items with reasons, `usage_recorded` token totals, and the worktree sweep result |
| alias | `/induct-quest-no-human` renders in all harness dirs and resolves; body is a pointer plus no-human rails, not a fork of induct |
| rename complete | `induct-solo` and the word `solo` for this mode are gone from skill dirs, code, and tests (the c1 `skills/induct-solo/` and its installed copies are removed/renamed, not left as a synonym) |

## Acceptance test (goal block)

- **Objective:** the queue runs itself; only judgment
  waits for a human.
- **Prove by:** skills tests for the alias and rails;
  one live no-human drive of a toy queue (two toy quests,
  one seeded to park) with its dawn report quoted.
- **Done when:** the alias is installed and the live
  drive parks the seeded quest, finishes the clean one,
  and reports both.

## Tests

known cases: the Acceptance table · property-based:
none — prose skill plus one live drive (stated
omission) · fixtures: skills tests, toy queue ·
demos: the live no-human drive, observed.

## Design question (owner, 2026-11-15 — settle in this exp)

Solo may be its own FSM rather than a mode of induct:
a queue-level machine (`queued -> preflight -> running
-> parked | finished -> reported`) sitting above the
exp FSM. Take the FSM shape if the rails (preflight,
parking, budget, dawn report) cannot be stated as
conductor rules over the existing exp FSM without
special cases; stay a skill mode if they can. The exp
must say which shape it shipped and why.

## Context

Red chair (2026-11-15) attacks that shaped this exp:
attestation forgery (no-human must park, never attest);
parallel queues multiplying the shared-tree branch
flip (desks only, one quest per checkout until proven
otherwise); "hopefully fleshed out" unmeasured
(preflight gate); unsupervised cycle burn (queue
budget); dawn needs data, not vibes (report from
`bp3 q r`, the registry, and `bp3 worktree list`).
